Good catch! The map controls have a higher z-index than the dropdown. Here's the fix - add this CSS at the end of your styles.css file:

```css
/* Fix z-index issues */
.species-select-container {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2000; /* Higher than map controls */
}

.species-dropdown {
    z-index: 2001; /* Even higher when open */
}

/* Keep map controls at a lower z-index */
.leaflet-control-container {
    z-index: 1000;
    position: relative;
}

/* Ensure the map itself doesn't block the dropdown */
.leaflet-pane {
    z-index: 1;
}

.leaflet-control {
    z-index: 1000;
}

.leaflet-top {
    z-index: 1000;
}

.leaflet-bottom {
    z-index: 1000;
}

/* Adjust dropdown position to be closer to the button */
.species-dropdown {
    margin-top: 2px; /* Reduce from 5px to 2px */
    max-height: 350px; /* Slightly reduce height if needed */
}
```

This CSS fix:

1. Increases the dropdown's z-index to 2000-2001 so it appears above the map controls
2. Keeps map controls at a lower z-index (1000) so they stay behind the dropdown
3. Reduces the margin between the button and dropdown from 5px to 2px, making it drop down less
4. Ensures all map layers and controls stay behind the species selector

The dropdown will now appear above the map controls instead of being hidden behind them, and it will be positioned slightly closer to the button.
